“My project is PortfolioPro, a stock market paper-trading and portfolio management system. 
The frontend is developed using Angular and the backend uses Java Spring Boot REST APIs.
 First, the user registers and logs in. 
 Authentication is handled using Spring Security and JWT.
  After login, the user can search for stocks and view market information obtained through a market-data API.
   The user can add stocks to a watchlist and perform simulated buy and sell transactions.
    These transactions are stored in MySQL using JPA and Hibernate.
     The system updates the user's holdings and calculates portfolio value and profit or loss.
      It also provides transaction history and can perform technical and portfolio-level analysis.
       Since it is a paper-trading system, no real money or brokerage transaction is involved.”

       